course: dictionary
lesson: 13378
title: Hazardous: dangerous things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Hazardous» is a tricky word, but the clues around it help. «The icy path was hazardous, so the bus stopped at the bottom of the hill.» Ice makes a path slippery, and the bus stopping tells you the path was not safe. Hazardous must mean dangerous.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it in. «The icy path was dangerous, so the bus stopped at the bottom of the hill.» It still makes sense, so dangerous is a good meaning. Hazardous is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like a hazardous road or hazardous chemicals.
explain: Warning signs often tell you that something is hazardous. «Keep hazardous cleaning liquids out of reach of children.» The words «out of reach» show that the liquid can cause harm, so keep it away from anyone who could get hurt.
fact: Hazardous means dangerous, likely to cause harm.
fact: «Hazardous» describes things that are risky to health or safety.
fact: Hazard symbols on labels show if something is toxic, flammable or corrosive.
fact: «Hazardous chemicals» must be kept out of reach of children.
fact: Hazardous is an adjective: hazardous, more hazardous, most hazardous.
exercise: «The icy path was hazardous, so we walked very slowly.» What does hazardous mean here? | Very long | Warm and sunny | *Dangerous and likely to cause harm | Smooth and clean
exercise: «Keep hazardous cleaning liquids out of reach of children.» What does this tell you to do? | Share them with your friends | Put them on a low shelf where they are easy to reach | *Keep them away, because they could cause harm | Taste a little to check them
exercise: «The weather report warned of hazardous roads.» Which word could replace hazardous? | Clean | Empty | *Dangerous | Funny
test: «The science teacher showed us a hazard symbol on the bottle.» What does the hazard symbol show? | That it is a toy | The bottle is empty | *That the substance could be harmful, such as toxic or flammable | That it tastes sweet
test: Which sentence uses hazardous correctly? | The soft pillow was hazardous. | The birthday cake was hazardous and sweet and cold. | *The broken glass on the floor was hazardous, so we swept it up. | The hazardous song made everyone smile.
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to hazardous? | Gentle | Bright | *Risky | Safe
